-- coa29-sch7.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), 2006 c. 46, SCHEDULE 7 "Parent and subsidiary undertakings: supplementary provisions".
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Generated by work/build.py from work/src/coa29-sch7.l4; quote lines are produced by srcrefs.py.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk (Open Government Licence v3.0) made by a converter script; it is
-- not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Line numbers are of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- TARGET. The stable `l4` (main) 1.6.110. No section GIVEN, no REFUSE, no sets, no TYPICALLY, no YMD.
--
-- WHAT THIS SCHEDULE DOES. Section 1162 (the keel's, coa-definitions.l4) says an undertaking is a parent undertaking of another if it holds a
-- majority of the voting rights (2)(a), is a member and may appoint or remove a majority of the board (2)(b), may exercise a dominant
-- influence by the articles or a control contract (2)(c), or is a member and controls a majority of the voting rights by agreement (2)(d).
-- This Schedule explains those expressions: which rights count and whose they are treated as being. It parallels Schedule 6 (the same
-- shape for companies) with three differences: para 2(2) (an undertaking with no general meetings), para 4 (dominant influence and the
-- control contract) and para 9(3) (a "group undertaking", s 1161(5)). Its answers are the facts the keel's `s 1162 relation` takes (PLAN.md
-- section 4.2): the lead wires them at the merge. No function is imported from the keel; no rule of s 1162 is restated here.
--
-- READING A RESULT (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): JUST TRUE = the text says the case is within the provision;
-- JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words (a "means"/"are to" definition, "unless", "only if", a flat negative, an unmet "where" or
-- "if"); NOTHING = the text does not decide (a rule limited by its own wording, "include", silent).

§ `Schedule 7 -- Parent and subsidiary undertakings: supplementary provisions`

-- Who holds a block of rights in the undertaking, seen from the parent undertaking (the undertaking that may be the parent).
DECLARE `sch 7 who holds the rights` IS ONE OF
    `sch 7 the parent undertaking itself`
    `sch 7 a subsidiary undertaking of the parent undertaking`
    `sch 7 someone else`

-- In what capacity they are held (paragraphs 6, 7 and 8).
DECLARE `sch 7 how the rights are held` IS ONE OF
    `sch 7 held beneficially`
    `sch 7 held in a fiduciary capacity`
    `sch 7 held as nominee for the parent undertaking`
    `sch 7 held as nominee for someone else`
    `sch 7 held by way of security provided by the parent undertaking`
    `sch 7 held by way of security provided by someone else`

§§ `Voting rights in an undertaking (para 2)`

-- src:19593 | 2 (1) In section 1162(2)(a) and (d) the references to the voting rights in an undertaking are to the rights conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares or, in the case of an undertaking not having a share capital, on members, to vote at general meetings of the undertaking on all, or substantially all, matters.
@ref sch 7 para 2(1) Voting rights in an undertaking (src:19593)
GIVEN `the undertaking has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights are conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights are conferred on members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights are to vote at general meetings of the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights are to vote on all, or substantially all, matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 2(1) the rights are voting rights in the undertaking` MEANS
    IF       `the rights are to vote at general meetings of the undertaking`
         AND `the rights are to vote on all, or substantially all, matters`
         AND (   (`the undertaking has a share capital` AND `the rights are conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares`)
              OR ((NOT (`the undertaking has a share capital`)) AND `the rights are conferred on members`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the references to the voting rights in an undertaking are to the rights conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares or, in the case of an undertaking not having a share capital, on members, to vote at general meetings of the undertaking on all, or substantially all, matters"

-- src:19594 | (2) In relation to an undertaking which does not have general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights the references to holding a majority of the voting rights in the undertaking shall be construed as references to having the right under the constitution of the undertaking to direct the overall policy of the undertaking or to alter the terms of its constitution.
@ref sch 7 para 2(2) An undertaking that has no general meetings (src:19594)
GIVEN `the undertaking has general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking has the right under its constitution to direct its overall policy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking has the right under its constitution to alter the terms of its constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 2(2) the undertaking holds a majority of the voting rights in the other undertaking` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking has general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In relation to an undertaking which does not have general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights"
    ELSE IF       `the undertaking has the right under its constitution to direct its overall policy`
              OR  `the undertaking has the right under its constitution to alter the terms of its constitution`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the references to holding a majority of the voting rights in the undertaking shall be construed as references to having the right under the constitution of the undertaking to direct the overall policy of the undertaking or to alter the terms of its constitution"

§§ `Right to appoint or remove a majority of the directors (para 3)`

-- src:19596 | 3 (1) In section 1162(2)(b) the reference to the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors is to the right to appoint or remove directors holding a majority of the voting rights at meetings of the board on all, or substantially all, matters.
@ref sch 7 para 3(1) A majority of the board of directors (src:19596)
GIVEN `the votes at meetings of the board held by the directors the right is a right to appoint or remove` IS A NUMBER
      `all the votes at meetings of the board` IS A NUMBER
      `the votes at meetings of the board are on all, or substantially all, matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 3(1) the right is a right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors` MEANS
    IF       `the votes at meetings of the board are on all, or substantially all, matters`
         AND `all the votes at meetings of the board` GREATER THAN 0
         AND (`the votes at meetings of the board held by the directors the right is a right to appoint or remove` TIMES 2) GREATER THAN `all the votes at meetings of the board`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the reference to the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors is to the right to appoint or remove directors holding a majority of the voting rights at meetings of the board on all, or substantially all, matters" (a majority read as more than half: fork)

-- src:19597 | (2) An undertaking shall be treated as having the right to appoint to a directorship if—
-- src:19598 | (a) a person's appointment to it follows necessarily from his appointment as director of the undertaking, or
-- src:19599 | (b) the directorship is held by the undertaking itself.
@ref sch 7 para 3(2) Treated as having the right to appoint to a directorship (src:19597-19599)
GIVEN `a person's appointment to the directorship follows necessarily from his appointment as director of the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directorship is held by the undertaking itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 3(2) the undertaking is treated as having the right to appoint to the directorship` MEANS
    IF       `a person's appointment to the directorship follows necessarily from his appointment as director of the undertaking`
         OR  `the directorship is held by the undertaking itself`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An undertaking shall be treated as having the right to appoint to a directorship if— (a) a person's appointment to it follows necessarily from his appointment as director of the undertaking, or (b) the directorship is held by the undertaking itself" (an unmet "if"; marginal reading (a))

-- src:19600 | (3) A right to appoint or remove which is exercisable only with the consent or concurrence of another person shall be left out of account unless no other person has a right to appoint or, as the case may be, remove in relation to that directorship.
@ref sch 7 para 3(3) A right exercisable only with consent or concurrence (src:19600)
GIVEN `the right is exercisable only with the consent or concurrence of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no other person has a right to appoint or, as the case may be, remove in relation to that directorship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 3(3) the right is taken into account` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the right is exercisable only with the consent or concurrence of another person`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A right to appoint or remove which is exercisable only with the consent or concurrence of another person shall be left out of account"
    ELSE IF `no other person has a right to appoint or, as the case may be, remove in relation to that directorship`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be left out of account unless no other person has a right to appoint or, as the case may be, remove in relation to that directorship"

§§ `Right to exercise dominant influence (para 4)`

-- src:19602 | 4 (1) For the purposes of section 1162(2)(c) an undertaking shall not be regarded as having the right to exercise a dominant influence over another undertaking unless it has a right to give directions with respect to the operating and financial policies of that other undertaking which its directors are obliged to comply with whether or not they are for the benefit of that other undertaking.
@ref sch 7 para 4(1) Dominant influence: the right to give directions (src:19602)
GIVEN `the undertaking has a right to give directions with respect to the operating and financial policies of the other undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors of the other undertaking are obliged to comply with the directions whether or not they are for the benefit of that other undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 4(1) the undertaking cannot be regarded as having the right to exercise a dominant influence` MEANS
    IF       `the undertaking has a right to give directions with respect to the operating and financial policies of the other undertaking`
         AND `the directors of the other undertaking are obliged to comply with the directions whether or not they are for the benefit of that other undertaking`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be regarded as having the right to exercise a dominant influence over another undertaking unless it has a right to give directions with respect to the operating and financial policies of that other undertaking which its directors are obliged to comply with whether or not they are for the benefit of that other undertaking" (the "unless" is met, so the bar does not apply; the text does not say that the undertaking IS regarded as having the right: fork)
    ELSE JUST TRUE -- the bar applies: "shall not be regarded as having the right to exercise a dominant influence over another undertaking unless ..."

-- src:19603 | (2) A “control contract” means a contract in writing conferring such a right which—
-- src:19604 | (a) is of a kind authorised by the articles of the undertaking in relation to which the right is exercisable, and
-- src:19605 | (b) is permitted by the law under which that undertaking is established.
@ref sch 7 para 4(2) A control contract (src:19603-19605)
GIVEN `the contract is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract confers such a right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is of a kind authorised by the articles of the undertaking in relation to which the right is exercisable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is permitted by the law under which that undertaking is established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 4(2) the contract is a control contract` MEANS
    IF       `the contract is in writing`
         AND `the contract confers such a right`
         AND `the contract is of a kind authorised by the articles of the undertaking in relation to which the right is exercisable`
         AND `the contract is permitted by the law under which that undertaking is established`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “control contract” means a contract in writing conferring such a right which— (a) is of a kind authorised by the articles of the undertaking in relation to which the right is exercisable, and (b) is permitted by the law under which that undertaking is established"

