-- src:19615 | (2) Rights shall be regarded as held as nominee for another if they are exercisable only on his instructions or with his consent or concurrence.
@ref sch 7 para 7(2) Regarded as held as nominee for another (src:19615)
GIVEN `the rights are exercisable only on his instructions or with his consent or concurrence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 7(2) the rights are regarded as held as nominee for another` MEANS
    IF `the rights are exercisable only on his instructions or with his consent or concurrence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rights shall be regarded as held as nominee for another if they are exercisable only on his instructions or with his consent or concurrence" (an unmet "if"; marginal reading (a); a nominee in the ordinary sense is the input of sub-paragraph (1))

-- src:19614 | 7 (1) Rights held by a person as nominee for another shall be treated as held by the other.
@ref sch 7 para 7(1) Rights held as nominee for another (src:19614)
GIVEN `the rights are held by a person as nominee for another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights are regarded as held as nominee for another under paragraph 7(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 7(1) the rights are treated as held by the other` MEANS
    IF       `the rights are held by a person as nominee for another`
