-- src:19623 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph 8 rights shall be treated as being exercisable in accordance with the instructions or in the interests of an undertaking if they are exercisable in accordance with the instructions of or, as the case may be, in the interests of any group undertaking.
-- src:19624 | Disregard of certain rights
-- src:19625 | 10 The voting rights in an undertaking shall be reduced by any rights held by the undertaking itself.
-- src:19626 | Supplementary
-- src:19627 | 11 References in any provision of paragraphs 6 to 10 to rights held by a person include rights falling to be treated as held by him by virtue of any other provision of those paragraphs but not rights which by virtue of any such provision are to be treated as not held by him.
@ref sch 7 paras 5 to 11 The block of rights is treated as held by the parent undertaking (src:19608-19627)
GIVEN `who holds the rights` IS A `sch 7 who holds the rights`
      `how the rights are held` IS A `sch 7 how the rights are held`
      `the result of sch 7 para 5` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the result of sch 7 para 8` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 paras 5 to 11 the rights are treated as held by the parent undertaking` MEANS
    IF `the result of sch 7 para 5` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rights which are exercisable only in certain circumstances shall be taken into account only— (a) when the circumstances have arisen ... or (b) when the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights"
    ELSE CONSIDER `how the rights are held`
         WHEN `sch 7 held beneficially` THEN
             CONSIDER `who holds the rights`
             WHEN `sch 7 the parent undertaking itself` THEN JUST TRUE -- the parent undertaking holds them itself (s 1162(2)(a)): this Schedule takes nothing away
             WHEN `sch 7 a subsidiary undertaking of the parent undertaking` THEN JUST TRUE -- para 9(1)
             WHEN `sch 7 someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): rights held beneficially by a third party are not attributed to the parent undertaking by this Schedule
         WHEN `sch 7 held in a fiduciary capacity` THEN
             CONSIDER `who holds the rights`
             WHEN `sch 7 the parent undertaking itself` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rights held by a person in a fiduciary capacity shall be treated as not held by him" (para 6)
             WHEN `sch 7 a subsidiary undertaking of the parent undertaking` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "treated as not held by him" (para 6), and not rights "treated as held by him" for para 9(1) (para 11)
             WHEN `sch 7 someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a third party's fiduciary holding is not attributed to the parent undertaking by this Schedule
         WHEN `sch 7 held as nominee for the parent undertaking` THEN JUST TRUE -- para 7(1): "treated as held by the other"
         WHEN `sch 7 held as nominee for someone else` THEN
             CONSIDER `who holds the rights`
             WHEN `sch 7 the parent undertaking itself` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rights held by a person as nominee for another shall be treated as held by the other" (para 7(1): the other is someone else)
             WHEN `sch 7 a subsidiary undertaking of the parent undertaking` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be treated as held by the other" (para 7(1)), and para 11: not rights treated as not held by the subsidiary undertaking
             WHEN `sch 7 someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a third party's nominee holding is not attributed to the parent undertaking by this Schedule
         WHEN `sch 7 held by way of security provided by the parent undertaking` THEN
             CONSIDER `who holds the rights`
             WHEN `sch 7 the parent undertaking itself` THEN JUST TRUE -- the parent undertaking holds the shares and also provides the security
             WHEN `sch 7 a subsidiary undertaking of the parent undertaking` THEN JUST TRUE -- para 8 (the provider) or para 9(1) (held by its subsidiary undertaking): either way the parent undertaking's
             WHEN `sch 7 someone else` THEN
                 CONSIDER `the result of sch 7 para 8`
                 WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- para 8: treated as held by the person providing the security
                 OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): para 8 attributes the rights to the provider only "where" its conditions (a) and (b) hold; otherwise they stay with the holder
         WHEN `sch 7 held by way of security provided by someone else` THEN
             CONSIDER `who holds the rights`
             WHEN `sch 7 someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a third party's security holding is not attributed to the parent undertaking by this Schedule
             OTHERWISE
                 CONSIDER `the result of sch 7 para 8`
                 WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rights attached to shares held by way of security shall be treated as held by the person providing the security" (para 8: held by that provider, not by the parent undertaking or its subsidiary undertaking)
                 WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE -- para 8 does not apply, so the holder keeps the rights (the parent undertaking's own, or its subsidiary undertaking's by para 9(1))
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph 8's conditions hold is not decided
